   "id": "rosh_hashanah.30a.18",
   "daf": "30a",
   "sentenceId": 17,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ וּמְנָלַן דְּעָבְדִינַן זֵכֶר לַמִּקְדָּשׁ? דְּאָמַר קְרָא: ״כִּי אַעֲלֶה אֲרוּכָה לָךְ וּמִמַּכּוֹתַיִךְ אֶרְפָּאֵךְ נְאֻם ה׳ כִּי נִדָּחָה קָרְאוּ לָךְ צִיּוֹן הִיא דּוֹרֵשׁ אֵין לָהּ״, מִכְּלַל דְּבָעֲיָא דְּרִישָׁה.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The Gemara asks: «And from where do we» derive «that one performs» actions in «commemoration of the Temple? As the verse states: “For I will restore health to you, and I will heal you of your wounds, said the Lord; because they have called you an outcast: She is Zion, there is none who care for her”» (Jeremiah 30:17). This verse teaches «by inference that» Jerusalem «requires caring» through acts of commemoration."
  }
